  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Upscaling UNESCO&apos;s efforts to the fight against racism and discriminat</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO has renewed its commitment to the compelling agenda of combatting racism and discrimination, and has engaged to address the Global Call against Racism contained in decision 210EX/5.I.B adopted in December 2020. The Global Call requested that the Organization develops a Roadmap &quot;to strengthen UNESCO&apos;s contribution to the fight against racism and discrimination across its field of competence&quot;, providing a strategic and operational framework to guide UNESCO&apos;s action in this important area, especially in the critical post-crisis period. The Roadmap is being developed by UNESCO in close consultation with its Members States and networks, including the International Coalition of Inclusive and Sustainable Cities - ICCAR, UNESCO Chairs, NGOs, scientific communities and other partners.</narrative>
  </description>
